# Pairs with RCommittedEventuallyVisible. The origin never ships the prepare of
# one participant, so the receiver leaf that owns it has no bucket when the
# saga's terminal arrives: it records the terminal and materialises nothing,
# and the committed saga's write never becomes visible there. The transport,
# the tally and the fairness are untouched; this is a protocol defect, and the
# liveness property reports it under the fairness the module asserts.
MODULE: RCommittedEventuallyVisiblePrepareNotShipped
TARGET: RCommittedEventuallyVisible
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: one participant's prepare is never written for replication, so its committed write never reaches the receiver
PERTURBS: OriginPrepare

--- FIND
    /\ outbox' = outbox \cup {Prep(k) : k \in XKeys}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: k2's prepare is not replicated.
    /\ outbox' = outbox \cup {Prep(k) : k \in XKeys \ {k2}}
--- END
